message: "Please cite this versioned research repository when using its code or data. The manuscript is a draft, not an accepted publication."
type: software
title: "Names and mechanistic interpretability: equivalent-name factual retrieval study"
authors:
  - family-names: Kendiukhov
    given-names: Ihor
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5342-1499"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Biodyn-AI/names-mechinterp"
url: "https://github.com/Biodyn-AI/names-mechinterp"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - language models
  - reference consistency
  - activation patching
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  Code, processed data, and a draft manuscript for a study of factual retrieval
  under equivalent contextual names in two instruction-tuned language models.
  Naming inconsistencies repeated in both models on 64 untouched scenarios under
  a publicly fixed plan. An unchanged internal repair corrected 16 of 40 complete
  wrong answers in 30 eligible fresh scenarios while preserving 50 correct answers;
  its practical usefulness remains uncertain. Earlier failed development tests
  are retained. Code is MIT-licensed;
  original data, documentation, and manuscript are CC BY 4.0.
